<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>Parallel optimization performance (q=10) of hypervolume metrics (<math id="A5.F11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math>) w.r.t. the number of observations (beyond initial points) on real-world applications. The solid line is the mean value averaged over 10 independent runs, and the shaded region is the standard deviation with 95% confidence around the mean value.</figcaption>
